    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0090" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg20"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Commercial Agreement/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-25T15:00:00-06:00">September 25, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. I brought to the attention of the Salvadoran Government orally and informally
                    the substance of the information contained in your circular telegram of
                    September 23, 2 p.m., and was informed that <pb facs="0091" n="21" xml:id="pg21"
                    /> this country has no representative at Geneva at this time. The proposition is
                    well understood by the Salvadoran Foreign Office the Undersecretary having been
                    present at Montevideo when it was under discussion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
